      "title": "DOWN TO EARTH: Less is so much more",
      "content_html": "Vanessa Moberg is the Cariboo Chilcotin Conservation Society's financial coordinator. After some recent decluttering Vanessa Moberg still kept a bag of tar sands, a sentimental reminder of her uncle and a practical reminder of the fossil fuels required to produce all her other stuff. Eager to declutter, I recently went through my boxes of sentimental items. “I’m a minimalist,” I thought. “This should be easy.” Before long, I found myself holding a Ziploc bag filled with a dark substance, and I thought, “Oh yeah! The tar sands my uncle gave me. Well, I can’t just throw out these perfectly good",
