      "title": "Astronomers track stellar merger as Andromeda giant engulfs companion",
      "content_html": "Astronomers have reconstructed the first observed case of a giant star engulfing its companion, tracking the pair through their merger in the Andromeda Galaxy. The system, AT 2025abao, began brightening in 2018 as the smaller star spiraled through the giant’s shared envelope of gas; the plunge ended in a powerful eruption in late 2025. The study appeared in the journal Nature on Nov. 18.\n\nThe analysis indicates the smaller star crashed into the giant’s core rather than surviving in a close orbit, but researchers say decades of further observations are needed to rule out a remnant. The observations recorded common-envelope evolution, a process used to explain how some binary stars tighten their orbits.",
