      "title": "Creality scanner requires wired PC connection for marker-free capture",
      "content_html": "Creality’s Raptor Pro Max, a recently launched handheld scanner for scanning automotive and other parts, can scan suitable black and metallic surfaces without scanning spray. Its marker-free blue-laser function works only with a wired connection to a PC; an optional Scan Bridge supports wireless scanning.\n\nThe scanner also has a near-infrared mode for scanning medium-to-large objects, faces and bodies, while its blue-laser modes target broad surfaces and small features such as edges and threads. Creality says its Creality Inspect software, which compares scans with reference computer-aided design (CAD) models, will be free for a limited time.",
